From 85b2f7a57345f195d88627840eaca7a19b8d7986 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Barnard <kevin.barnard@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 02:23:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] [minixrs] Driver: pin the image base at 0x100000

lld's default aarch64 image base is 0x200000, which is exactly the VA minixrs
maps every process's initial stack page at (SERVER_STACK_VA,
kernel/src/arch/aarch64/userland.rs). load_exec_image maps the PT_LOADs first
and the stack second, so a default-linked binary does not corrupt itself -- it
never runs at all: the stack's map_page lands on the image's own page, fails
AlreadyMapped, and the load unwinds to None (ENOMEM from exec, or a boot-time
"server image load failed").

Pin the base at the 0x100000 that servers/*/user.ld already uses. Processes can
share the VA because each gets its own TTBR0. That leaves the image 1 MiB
before it reaches the stack page; one whose PT_LOADs reach 0x200000 collides
and is rejected the same way.

This goes in the driver rather than in a linker script or the build scripts
because it *is* the milestone, not an implementation detail of it: those would
fix the binary while leaving M3's actual claim -- that a bare
"clang --target=aarch64-unknown-minixrs hello.c -o hello" suffices -- false.

Emitted unconditionally, with no suppression check for a user --image-base.
None is needed: lld resolves the option with getLastArg, so the last spelling
wins, and both -T (OPT_T_Group) and -Wl, args (AddLinkerInputs) render after
the driver's own flags. A condition would be untested policy over documented
behaviour. Under -r lld forces imageBase to 0 (lld/ELF/Writer.cpp), so the flag
is inert there -- as are the two -z flags above it, which are unconditional for
the same reason.

The override run asserts that by order rather than by negation: a CHECK-NOT
would have to exclude the very string the driver legitimately emits, so both
bases are matched positionally with CHECK-SAME.

Mutation-tested from the source side. Without the push_back the main run fails,
and the override run fails on its *first* CHECK-BASE-OVERRIDE-SAME
("--image-base=0x100000") rather than the second -- the evidence that it tests
the driver's own flag and not merely an echo of the user's.

check-clang-driver: 1403 tests, 1320 passed, 82 unsupported, 1 XFAIL, 0
failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/MinixRS.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c             | 12 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

diff --git a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/MinixRS.cpp b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/MinixRS.cpp
index b4dcfac6c661..84dd871a8930 100644
--- a/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/MinixRS.cpp
+++ b/clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/MinixRS.cpp
@@ -68,6 +68,20 @@ void minixrs::Linker::ConstructJob(Compilation &C, const JobAction &JA,
   CmdArgs.push_back("-z");
   CmdArgs.push_back("separate-loadable-segments");
 
+  // minixrs maps every process's initial stack page at SERVER_STACK_VA =
+  // 0x0020_0000 (kernel/src/arch/aarch64/userland.rs), which is exactly lld's
+  // default aarch64 image base. load_exec_image maps the PT_LOADs first and
+  // the stack second, so a default-linked binary does not corrupt anything --
+  // it never runs at all: the stack's map_page lands on the image's own page,
+  // fails AlreadyMapped, and the load unwinds to None (ENOMEM from exec, or a
+  // boot-time "server image load failed"). Pin the base at the 0x0010_0000
+  // that servers/*/user.ld already uses; processes can share it because each
+  // has its own TTBR0. That leaves the image 1 MiB of VA: one whose PT_LOADs
+  // reach 0x0020_0000 collides with the stack and is rejected the same way.
+  // This belongs in the driver rather than in a linker script so that a bare
+  // clang invocation stays sufficient (tooling/docs/plans/musl-m3.md).
+  CmdArgs.push_back("--image-base=0x100000");
+
   CmdArgs.push_back("--eh-frame-hdr");
 
   if (Args.hasArg(options::OPT_s))
diff --git a/clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c b/clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c
index df0eb65672c9..114c153f67ff 100644
--- a/clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c
+++ b/clang/test/Driver/minixrs.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 // PT_LOAD (minixrs D13).
 // CHECK-SAME: "-z" "max-page-size=4096"
 // CHECK-SAME: "-z" "separate-loadable-segments"
+// CHECK-SAME: "--image-base=0x100000"
 
 // crt1.o is the C-side brand emitter, so it has to come from the sysroot and
 // not from a host toolchain.
@@ -88,3 +89,14 @@
 // RUN: not %clang -### %s --target=aarch64-unknown-minixrs -fsanitize=address 2>&1 \
 // RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=CHECK-NO-SANITIZER %s
 // CHECK-NO-SANITIZER: error: unsupported option '-fsanitize=address' for target 'aarch64-unknown-minixrs'
+
+// A user --image-base is not suppressed, it is outranked: lld takes the last
+// spelling (getLastArg), and -Wl, args render after the driver's own flags.
+// Asserted positionally with CHECK-SAME rather than with a -NOT, which would
+// have to exclude the very string the driver legitimately emits.
+// RUN: %clang -### %s --target=aarch64-unknown-minixrs \
+// RUN:     -Wl,--image-base=0x400000 2>&1 \
+// RUN:     | FileCheck --check-prefix=CHECK-BASE-OVERRIDE %s
+// CHECK-BASE-OVERRIDE: {{.*}}ld.lld
+// CHECK-BASE-OVERRIDE-SAME: "--image-base=0x100000"
+// CHECK-BASE-OVERRIDE-SAME: "--image-base=0x400000"
